{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/844011-opinions-wanted-on-this-hedge-beast-companion","id":844011,"title":"Opinions wanted on this Hedge Beast Companion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-08T09:38:49-08:00","id":844011,"title":"Opinions wanted on this Hedge Beast Companion","content":"Hello everyone. I've just finished statting up my first Hedge Beast Companion and I wanted to see if people more experienced with Changeling could give some advice for how to make the creature more thematically appropriate for the concept I'm going for. <br /> <br /> The beast is a bird made entirely out of blue coins. It is supposed to be a Blue Bird of Fortune. It is decently knowledgeable about Changelings due to previously serving as a companion to a spring courtier several years ago (hedge years) but got separate from them when a Keeper appeared. The other changeling is presumed dead or captured, but I'm leaving that door open for the STs in my game to use that section of the backstory as a plot hook. The bird got captured by hobs a while back and my character is going to barter with them in order to free it. <br /> <br /> Here is the character sheet I have written up:<br /> <br /> <u>Creature Concept</u>: Blue Bird of Fortune (3 dot Hedge Beast Companion<br /> <u>Nick Name</u>: Penny<br /> <br /> <u>Attributes</u>:<br /> <b>Mental:</b><br /> Intelligence: 2<br /> Wits: 4<br /> Resolve: 2<br /> <b>Physical:</b><br /> Strength: 1<br /> Dexterity: 4<br /> Stamina: 3<br /> <b>Social:</b><br /> Presence: 1<br /> Manipulation: 1<br /> Composure: 3<br /> <br /> <u>Derived Traits:</u><br /> Speed: 5+species factor<br /> Size: 1<br /> Defense: 4+<br /> Initiative: 7<br /> Health Boxes: 4<br /> Willpower: 5/5<br /> <br /> <u>Skills:</u><br /> <b>Mental: 5</b><br /> Academics: 0<br /> Crafts: 0<br /> Investigation: 2<br /> Medicine: 0<br /> Occult: 3<br /> Politics: 0<br /> Science: 0<br /> <b> Physical: 10</b><br /> Athletics: 3<br /> Brawl: 0<br /> Ride: 0<br /> Firearms: 0<br /> Larceny: 1<br /> Stealth: 3<br /> Survival: 3<br /> Weaponry: 0<br /> <b> Social: 9</b><br /> Animal Ken: 3<br /> Empathy: 1<br /> Expression: 1<br /> Intimidation: 0<br /> Persuasion: 1<br /> Socialize: 1<br /> Streetwise: 1<br /> Subterfuge:1<br /> <br /> <u>Wyrd</u>: 3<br /> Glamour: 12<br /> <br /> <u>Merits:</u><br /> Eidetic Memory 2<br /> Allies \u2013 Birds: 3<br /> Perfect Stillness: 1<br /> Market Sense: 1<br /> Resources: 2<br /> <br /> <u>Contracts</u>:<br /> Dreaming 1<br /> Hearth 4<br /> Fang and Talon 1 - Birds<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:56:04-08:00","id":844019,"title":"","content":"Where do you get the stats for animals, the CoD is supposed to have it, but I can't find them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:18:34-08:00","id":844033,"title":"","content":"How does your bird have Occult, etc. When none of the stock animals do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:19:05-08:00","id":844034,"title":"","content":"Oh this is 1e. Duh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T11:05:10-08:00","id":844058,"title":"","content":"I think it looks fine, but I'm not sure what you want out of a &quot;Blue Bird of Fortune.&quot; Presumably luck, so Hearth Contracts were a good call, and having money, so yay Resources. For its time with the Spring Courtier, did it just pick up knowledge about Changelings generally, or did it learn about the internal politics/strife/secrets of the Freehold? If the latter, I'd move some Occult to Politics, maybe replace the Allies with Contacts in the Courts. I don't know if the concept calls for Eidetic Memory, because birds and fortune are rather flighty.<br /> <br /> CoD animal stats are <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xMwKNrnxhEuCQjP1qStbxl-C4JIyRmT1D4FVgSqjmpo/edit\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, which may help; ravens/crows apparently have a speed factor of 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T12:08:55-08:00","id":844087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/844011-opinions-wanted-on-this-hedge-beast-companion?p=844058#post844058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it looks fine, but I'm not sure what you want out of a &amp;quot;Blue Bird of Fortune.&amp;quot; Presumably luck, so Hearth Contracts were a good call, and having money, so yay Resources. For its time with the Spring Courtier, did it just pick up knowledge about Changelings generally, or did it learn about the internal politics/strife/secrets of the Freehold? If the latter, I'd move some Occult to Politics, maybe replace the Allies with Contacts in the Courts. I don't know if the concept calls for Eidetic Memory, because birds and fortune are rather flighty.<br /> <br /> CoD animal stats are <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xMwKNrnxhEuCQjP1qStbxl-C4JIyRmT1D4FVgSqjmpo/edit&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, which may help; ravens/crows apparently have a speed factor of 10.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you very much. Still it should have been included in the CoD corebook, people who don't visit these forums won't have access to this. Great book, but this is a major oversight IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}